{"term":"supervise","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d30c2a0f2a70f2f70e","definition":"To oversee or direct (a task or organization).","example":"Without someone to supervise them, the group will lack direction.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["superintend"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cosupervise","supervisable","supervisal","supervisive"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supervise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9b18c3636f3ca5e166","definition":"To oversee a task, organization, etc.; to provide supervision; to act as a supervisor.","example":"Under the Medicare Benefits Schedule, doctors can’t claim payment from the government for a Covid-19 vaccination provided in their clinic by a nurse, unless a GP is on the premises to supervise.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["superintend"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["cosupervise","supervisable","supervisal","supervisive"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supervise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be5a526aaf70500d15","definition":"To look over so as to read; to peruse.","example":"Let me supervise the canzonet.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["superintend"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["cosupervise","supervisable","supervisal","supervisive"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supervise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈsuː.pə.vaɪz/"},"wordFamily":["cosupervise","supervisable","supervisal","supervisive"]}